      "dcterms:title": "KNOT CABLING AND THE DEGREE OF THE COLORED JONES",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "II, POLYNOMIAL"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20211110",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1501.04614",
      "dcterms:abstract": "We continue our study of the degree of the colored Jones polynomial under knot cabling started in [8]. Under certain hypothesis on this degree, we determine how the Jones slopes and the linear term behave under cabling. As an application we verify Garoufalidis’ Slope Conjecture and a conjecture of [8] for cables of a two-parameter family of closed 3-braids called 2-fusion knots.",
